Merge Conflicts

What Causes Conflicts
Conflicts occur when: - Same lines modified in both branches - File deleted in one branch, modified in another - File renamed differently in both branches


Conflict Example
File content in main branch:
function greet(name) {
    return "Hello, " + name + "!";
}
File content in feature branch:
function greet(name) {
    return "Hi there, " + name + "!";
}


Conflict Markers
When conflict occurs, Git adds conflict markers:
function greet(name) {
&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt; HEAD
    return "Hello, " + name + "!";
=======
    return "Hi there, " + name + "!";
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; feature-branch
}
Conflict markers explained: - &lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt; HEAD: Start of current branch content - =======: Separator between conflicting content - &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; branch-name: End of merging branch content

